00:36:22.070 --> 00:36:24.621
You have relationships
with key partners and ISVs.

00:36:24.621 --> 00:36:26.870
And you want to make sure
that everything plays nicely

00:36:26.870 --> 00:36:28.744
together and you want
to make sure, also,

00:36:28.744 --> 00:36:31.160
that you're not getting locked
into any decision you make.

00:36:34.120 --> 00:36:36.760
So the first step is typically
to extend your network

00:36:36.760 --> 00:36:38.030
into Google Cloud Platform.

00:36:38.030 --> 00:36:41.230
And we have a number of
ways that you can do this.

00:36:41.230 --> 00:36:45.040
We have Carrier Interconnect
which provides enterprise grade

00:36:45.040 --> 00:36:47.740
connections to Google using
Interconnect Carrier Service

00:36:47.740 --> 00:36:49.240
provider partners.

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:50.890
You can also do
Direct Peering which

00:36:50.890 --> 00:36:53.140
allows you to connect
directly to Google

00:36:53.140 --> 00:36:55.060
for high levels of traffic.

00:36:55.060 --> 00:36:56.830
And then we're,
very soon this year,

00:36:56.830 --> 00:36:59.230
going to be rolling out Private
Interconnect and Partner

00:36:59.230 --> 00:37:03.190
Interconnect which allows
easy RFC 1918 private

00:37:03.190 --> 00:37:06.709
addressing to be used on GCP.

00:37:06.709 --> 00:37:09.250
Of course, all of your data and
all your internet connections

00:37:09.250 --> 00:37:13.060
can be secured via VPN and you
can segment off your network

00:37:13.060 --> 00:37:17.597
from the outside world in
our Virtual Private Cloud.

