are very important
in this space,

00:37:50.990 --> 00:37:52.970
for example, CrowdStrike.

00:37:52.970 --> 00:37:56.840
CrowdStrike, as organizations
move their sensitive data

00:37:56.840 --> 00:38:00.350
and computing capabilities
to Google Cloud Platform,

00:38:00.350 --> 00:38:01.850
they need to protect
the endpoints

00:38:01.850 --> 00:38:03.530
in a hybrid environment.

00:38:03.530 --> 00:38:05.990
So CrowdStrike has
a Falcon Platform,

00:38:05.990 --> 00:38:08.440
which is a next generation
endpoint protection

00:38:08.440 --> 00:38:10.760
and it enables customers
to seamlessly migrate

00:38:10.760 --> 00:38:13.460
their on-prem
security to the cloud.

00:38:13.460 --> 00:38:15.562
Falcon is a Cloud
native ecosystem

00:38:15.562 --> 00:38:17.270
and provides continuous
threat protection

00:38:17.270 --> 00:38:20.849
from malware, non malware
threats on endpoints

00:38:20.849 --> 00:38:23.390
and servers, regardless of where
they are physically located,

00:38:23.390 --> 00:38:27.690
be they on the network
or hosted in GCP.

00:38:27.690 --> 00:38:32.080
Likewise, Trend Micro has a deep
security hybrid cloud solution,

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:34.620
which enables organizations
to securely move

00:38:34.620 --> 00:38:37.650
to the Google Cloud Platform
without compromising security.

00:38:37.650 --> 00:38:40.110
It helps organizations meet
their shared responsibility

00:38:40.110 --> 00:38:42.650
in the cloud by offering
dev apps friendly workload

00:38:42.650 --> 00:38:46.190
protection, a uniform security
visibility and management

00:38:46.190 --> 00:38:48.780
of on-prem virtualized
public cloud,

00:38:48.780 --> 00:38:52.710
and multiple security controls
to speed compliance virtually

00:38:52.710 --> 00:38:55.132
patched against
vulnerabilities and proactively

00:38:55.132 --> 00:38:57.090
defend against network
and application threats.

00:39:00.380 --> 00:39:03.820
And I want to sort of wrap up
the talk on Google's philosophy

00:39:03.820 --> 00:39:06.830
on open source and open APIs.

00:39:06.830 --> 00:39:10.430
This is absolutely
critical to our story.

00:39:10.430 --> 00:39:12.380
You know, recent
research suggests

00:39:12.380 --> 00:39:16.660
that 82% of enterprises
have a hybrid cloud strategy

00:39:16.660 --> 00:39:21.410
and that includes 1.5 public
and 1.7 private clouds.

00:39:21.410 --> 00:39:24.200
And Google Cloud's
vision is to really help

00:39:24.200 --> 00:39:28.580
customers to succeed in
an open multi-cloud world.

00:39:28.580 --> 00:39:32.450
Over our history, we've released
over 20 million lines of code,

00:39:32.450 --> 00:39:35.180
projects like Chromium,
TensorFlow, Kubernetes,

00:39:35.180 --> 00:39:38.120
and so on, and we've incubated
a number of other projects

00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:43.290
which have led to innovations
like Hadoop, HSpace, and so on.

00:39:43.290 --> 00:39:48.150
So it's this devotion to open
source and open APIs that

00:39:48.150 --> 00:39:51.390
means that customers can
continue to drive innovation,

00:39:51.390 --> 00:39:54.390
without feeling locked
into Cloud Platform.

00:39:54.390 --> 00:39:57.000
You can bring your
applications to Cloud,

00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:59.520
but you can also run
those same applications

00:39:59.520 --> 00:40:01.730
on premise or on another cloud.

00:40:01.730 --> 00:40:03.480
And we believe that
being open is the best

00:40:03.480 --> 00:40:06.930
way to achieve these hybrid
multi-cloud strategies

00:40:06.930 --> 00:40:08.610
and we're committed
to helping customers

00:40:08.610 --> 00:40:11.500
leverage these architectures
in a flexible and low risk way.

00:40:14.260 --> 00:40:18.520
So with that, I just wanted
to tell everyone, again,

00:40:18.520 --> 00:40:21.460
that we're committed to
helping to get your journey

00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:24.060
to be secure to
Google Cloud Platform.

